# 🔋 Smart Battery Management System (BMS) with Cell Balancing using ESP32
## 📌 Project Overview
This project is a Smart Battery Management System (BMS) developed using an ESP32 for a 2S Lithium-Ion battery pack. The main aim of the project is to monitor important battery parameters, 
provide protection against unsafe conditions, and maintain better cell voltage balance.
The system monitors individual cell voltage, total battery voltage, current, temperature, and State of Charge (SoC) in real time. Passive cell balancing is implemented using MOSFETs and resistors. 
The ESP32 also provides Wi-Fi connectivity for IoT-based battery monitoring through ThingSpeak.

## 🎯 Objectives
- Monitor individual cell and total battery voltage
- Monitor charging/discharging current
- Monitor battery temperature
- Estimate State of Charge (SoC)
- Perform passive cell balancing
- Protect the battery from abnormal operating conditions
- Display battery parameters in real time
- Enable remote monitoring using IoT

---

## ⚙️ Key Features

- Real-time cell voltage monitoring
- Total battery voltage monitoring
- Current monitoring using ACS712
- Temperature monitoring using DS18B20
- State of Charge (SoC) estimation
- MOSFET-based passive cell balancing
- Overvoltage protection
- Undervoltage protection
- Overcurrent protection
- Over-temperature protection
- Severe cell imbalance detection
- Relay-based protection
- 16×2 I2C LCD display
- ESP32 Wi-Fi connectivity
- ThingSpeak-based remote monitoring

