## 🔄 Working Principle

The ESP32 acts as the main controller of the BMS and continuously collects battery parameters from the connected sensors.

The total battery voltage is measured through a voltage divider, while the first cell voltage is measured separately. The second cell voltage is obtained from the total battery voltage and cell 1 voltage.

The ACS712 sensor measures the battery current and the DS18B20 sensor monitors battery temperature.

The measured parameters are processed by the ESP32 and checked against predefined safety limits. If an unsafe condition such as overvoltage, undervoltage, overcurrent, excessive temperature, or severe cell imbalance is detected, the relay is controlled to disconnect the battery/load.

The system also estimates the State of Charge (SoC) using the measured battery parameters.

---

## 🔋 Passive Cell Balancing

Cell balancing is required because cells connected in series may develop different voltage levels during charging and discharging.

In this project, passive cell balancing is used.

When the voltage difference between the two cells exceeds the defined balancing threshold, the corresponding MOSFET is switched ON. The excess energy from the higher-voltage cell is dissipated through a balancing resistor.

This helps reduce the voltage difference between the cells and improves the overall operation of the battery pack.

### Balancing Method

**Passive balancing → MOSFET + Resistor**

---

## 🛡️ Battery Protection

The system continuously checks for abnormal battery conditions.

| Condition | Protection |
|---|---|
| Overvoltage | Relay protection |
| Undervoltage | Relay protection |
| Overcurrent | Relay protection |
| High Temperature | Relay protection |
| Severe Cell Imbalance | Fault detection |
| Reverse Current | Fault detection |

When a fault condition is detected, the ESP32 changes the relay state to disconnect the protected circuit.

---

## 📊 Parameters Monitored

- Cell 1 Voltage
- Cell 2 Voltage
- Total Battery Voltage
- Current
- Temperature
- State of Charge (SoC)
- Cell Voltage Difference
- Balancing Status
- Fault Status

---

## 🌐 IoT Monitoring

The ESP32's built-in Wi-Fi capability can be used to send battery data to the ThingSpeak cloud platform.

This allows parameters such as voltage, current, temperature, and SoC to be monitored remotely and visualized through graphs.

